 Drills: set `OUTBOUND_FAIL=<destination>[,<destination>]` to make deliveries to those[m[m
 destinations fail with `DeliveryError`.[m[m
[32m+[m[m
[32m+[m[32m## Failed-job incidents[m[m
[32m+[m[m
[32m+[m[32mAfter the final failed attempt, the runner sends an incident to `tracker` (Faultline).[m[m
[32m+[m[32mSuccessful runs do not send incidents. The failed oplog entry records `incident` as[m[m
[32m+[m[32m`sent`, `suppressed`, or `undelivered`; tracker outages do not change the job's exit code.[m[m
[32m+[m[m
[32m+[m[32m`var/incidents.json` keeps per-fingerprint occurrence counts, the first failure time, and[m[m
[32m+[m[32mlast successful send time (`null` until delivered). Repeats within[m[m
[32m+[m[32m`incident.dedupe_window_minutes` of the last successful send are counted but suppressed.[m[m
[32m+[m[32mThe window uses the run's `--now` clock, not wall time. Failed deliveries count too, but[m[m
[32m+[m[32mnever advance the last successful send time.[m[m
[32m+[m[m
[32m+[m[32mIncidents include the final attempt's last `incident.log_tail_lines` lines and the job's[m[m
[32m+[m[32msettings. Settings outside the tracker's accepted schema classes are masked; the ledger[m[m
[32m+[m[32mDSN is projected to its scheme/host/port/database, without credentials or query parameters,[m[m
[32m+[m[32mso on-call can still identify the replica. Restricted setting values (including Risk notes[m[m
[32m+[m[32mand encoded/decoded ledger passwords) are also scrubbed from outbound diagnostics. This[m[m
[32m+[m[32mprojection does not change the settings or logs used by the job itself.[m[m
